<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices remained firm on poor arrivals in central Indian markets on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices rose by 50-100 rupees per tonne. Arrivals were around 2,000 tonnes in the markets of central India while business volumes were dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were almost steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $291 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $111-112 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,750-3,800 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume were at lowest levels. The undertone was steady.</p>
